     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Hi Emma,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">I am not familiar with NHANES data but if the recordings per individual are split across multiple files then it sounds like you need GGIR parameter <a href=\"https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/GGIRParameters.html#maxrecordinginterval\" title=\"maxRecordingInterval\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://wadpac.github.io/GGIR/articles/GGIRParameters.html%23maxrecordinginterval&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488943413000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZP0vxB1-mYLwcQGfW0BT-\">maxRecordingInterval</a>, which makes that GGIR appends the files for you. All you need to do is make sure that the participant ID is consistently available in the filename such that GGIR knows which files below to the same participant.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Vincent</div><div>\r\n        On Sunday, 13 October 2024 at 5:25 PM, Emma Guyonnet &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">emmagu...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>\r\n        <blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n            <font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\">Hello everyone,</font><div><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\">I&#39;m trying to analyze the 2011-2014 NHANES raw physical activity monitor data (2011-2012: <a rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" href=\"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Nhanes/2011-2012/PAX80_G.htm\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Nhanes/2011-2012/PAX80_G.htm&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488943413000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jMIMrKhgYZlCftZbYHgMu\">https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Nhanes/2011-2012/PAX80_G.htm</a>). From previous posts, I saw that it is best to merge all .csv files per participant and then apply GGIR to the combined files. </font></div><div><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\">However, it looks like the HEADER_TIMESTAMP is in a character format because I keep getting the error: </font></div><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\">&quot;character string is not in a standard unambiguous format&quot; $call as.POSIXlt.character(x, tz, ...)&quot;</font></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\">I tried different methods to convert the timestamp variable to numeric in R, but I keep getting this error. </font></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial\">Any guidance on how to fix this error in R would be much appreciated. Thank you so much!</font></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(59,64,69)\"><br></p></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;R package GGIR&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" data-email-masked>RpackageGGIR...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/8981021e-3e51-4853-bb3c-1835133cee66n%40googlegroups.com\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/8981021e-3e51-4853-bb3c-1835133cee66n%2540googlegroups.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488943413000&amp;usg=AOvVaw17PiKU63lz5lrPMN1IZsiq\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/RpackageGGIR/8981021e-3e51-4853-bb3c-1835133cee66n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n\r\n        </blockquote><br>\r\n    </div>"
